# wavefront_shade.ckir - CEIR-19c STAGE 2 (the WAVEFRONT): the SHADE kernel. One thread per COMPACTED hit slot: re-derives the
# hit position o+t*d from the ray buffer + hit_t (NO stored hitpos — smaller queue; t crosses as an f32 but feeds only the
# shadow-ray ORIGIN, decision-robust on a clean-separation scene), casts a shadow ray toward a BAKED light L=(0,8,0) as
# P + s*(L-P) with tmax<1 (so the light itself is not an occluder — no normalize/length), and writes the lit/shadowed DECISION
# (1 = a shadow-ray MISS = unshadowed = lit). AUTHORED (mandate #1: NO C++ builder; the .ckir is the SOLE source). local_size=1
# (slot = WorkgroupIndex; the harness dispatches groups=count). BINDING CONTRACT: TLAS@0 (REAL — shadow rays), compacted@1
# (read: hit ray indices), rays@2 (read: 6 f32/ray), hit_t@3 (read: F32 distance), decision@4 (write: U32 1 lit / 0 shadowed).
schema = 1

